1	# Development Guide
2	
3	This guide covers local development setup, testing, and contributing to the project.
4	
5	## Prerequisites
6	
7	- Python 3.10+
8	- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (recommended) or pip
9	- A SemaphoreUI instance for testing
10	
11	## Local Setup
12	
13	```bash
14	# Clone the repository
15	git clone https://github.com/cloin/semaphore-mcp.git
16	cd semaphore-mcp
17	
18	# Create virtual environment and install dependencies
19	uv venv && source .venv/bin/activate
20	uv pip install -e ".[dev]"
21	
22	# Install pre-commit hooks
23	pre-commit install
24	```
25	
26	## Running Locally
27	
28	The server supports two transport modes:
29	
30	### STDIO Mode (Default)
31	
32	Used for direct integration with MCP clients like Claude Desktop:
33	
34	```bash
35	semaphore-mcp --url http://localhost:3000 --token your-token
36	```
37	
38	### HTTP Mode
39	
40	Used for network-accessible deployments:
41	
42	```bash
43	semaphore-mcp --transport http --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 \
44	  --url http://localhost:3000 --token your-token
45	```
46	
47	### Environment Variables
48	
49	You can also configure via environment variables:
50	
51	```bash
52	export SEMAPHORE_URL=http://localhost:3000
53	export SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token
54	export MCP_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG  # For verbose logging
55	
56	semaphore-mcp
57	```
58	
59	## Claude Desktop Configuration (Local Development)
60	
61	For local development with STDIO mode, configure Claude Desktop to use your virtual environment directly:
62	
63	**Config file locations:**
64	- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
65	- Windows: `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`
66	- Linux: `~/.config/claude-desktop/claude_desktop_config.json`
67	
68	```json
69	{
70	  "mcpServers": {
71	    "semaphore": {
72	      "command": "/path/to/semaphore-mcp/.venv/bin/semaphore-mcp",
73	      "args": [],
74	      "env": {
75	        "SEMAPHORE_URL": "http://localhost:3000",
76	        "SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN": "your-token-here"
77	      }
78	    }
79	  }
80	}
81	```
82	
83	## Setting Up a Test SemaphoreUI Instance
84	
85	```bash
86	docker run -d \
87	  --name semaphore-dev \
88	  -p 3000:3000 \
89	  -e SEMAPHORE_DB_DIALECT=bolt \
90	  -e SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin123 \
91	  -e SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_NAME=admin \
92	  -e SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@localhost \
93	  -e SEMAPHORE_ADMIN=admin \
94	  -v semaphore-data:/etc/semaphore \
95	  semaphoreui/semaphore:latest
96	```
97	
98	Then:
99	1. Access http://localhost:3000
100	2. Login with `admin` / `admin123`
101	3. Go to User Settings and create an API token
102	
103	## Testing
104	
105	For comprehensive testing documentation, see [TESTING.md](TESTING.md).
106	
107	**Quick commands:**
108	
109	```bash
110	# Run unit tests
111	uv run pytest tests/ --ignore=tests/e2e/ -v
112	
113	# Run E2E tests (requires Docker)
114	./scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh
115	
116	# Run with coverage
117	uv run pytest --cov=semaphore_mcp --cov-report=term-missing
118	```
119	
120	## Code Quality
121	
122	```bash
123	# Linting
124	ruff check src/ tests/
125	
126	# Formatting
127	ruff format src/ tests/
128	
129	# Fix linting issues automatically
130	ruff check --fix src/ tests/
131	
132	# Run all checks via pre-commit
133	pre-commit run --all-files
134	```
135	
136	## Building Docker Image Locally
137	
138	```bash
139	docker build -t semaphore-mcp:local .
140	
141	# Test the local image
142	docker run --rm -e SEMAPHORE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:3000 \
143	  -e SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token \
144	  -p 8000:8000 \
145	  semaphore-mcp:local
146	```
147	
148	## Project Structure
149	
150	```
151	semaphore-mcp/
152	├── src/semaphore_mcp/
153	│   ├── __init__.py
154	│   ├── api.py              # SemaphoreUI API client
155	│   ├── config.py           # Configuration management
156	│   ├── server.py           # FastMCP server implementation
157	│   ├── scripts/
158	│   │   └── start_server.py # CLI entry point
159	│   └── tools/              # MCP tool implementations
160	│       ├── base.py
161	│       ├── projects.py
162	│       ├── templates.py
163	│       ├── tasks.py
164	│       ├── environments.py
165	│       └── repositories.py
166	├── tests/
167	├── Dockerfile
168	├── pyproject.toml
169	└── README.md
170	```
171	
172	## Contributing
173	
174	1. Fork the repository
175	2. Create a feature branch (`git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`)
176	3. Make your changes and add tests
177	4. Run the test suite (`pytest`)
178	5. Run linting (`pre-commit run --all-files`)
179	6. Commit your changes (`git commit -m 'Add amazing feature'`)
180	7. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/amazing-feature`)
181	8. Open a Pull Request
182	
183	## GitHub Actions CI/CD
184	
185	If contributing, ensure the repository has these secrets configured for CI:
186	
187	- `ADMIN_USERNAME`: SemaphoreUI admin username (e.g., "admin")
188	- `ADMIN_PASSWORD`: SemaphoreUI admin password (e.g., "admin123")
189	
190	These are used for integration tests in CI. Local development can use environment variables or `.env` files.
191	
192	## Troubleshooting
193	
194	### Connection refused to SemaphoreUI
195	- Ensure SemaphoreUI is running on the configured URL
196	- Check firewall settings if using remote SemaphoreUI
197	- Verify the URL format (include `http://` or `https://`)
198	
199	### Authentication errors
200	- Regenerate your API token in SemaphoreUI User Settings
201	- Ensure the token is correctly set in your environment
202	- Check that the user account has appropriate permissions
203	
204	### Claude Desktop not connecting
205	- Verify the absolute path in your config is correct
206	- Test the command manually in terminal first
207	- Check Claude Desktop logs for specific error messages
208	- Ensure virtual environment has all required dependencies
209	
210	### Debug Mode
211	
212	Enable detailed logging:
213	```bash
214	export MCP_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
215	semaphore-mcp
216	```
217	

